OL,3,AMore than 100,000 people in Japan are
OL,4,Anow aged 100 or older
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe number of people aged 100 or more
OL,7,Fin Japan has exceeded 100,000 for the
OL,8,Ffirst time, according to the health
OL,9,Fministry.
OL,11,FFigures show Japan is now home to
OL,12,F107,677 centenarians, the highest
OL,13,Fnumber in the world, of which 88% are
OL,14,Fwomen. The oldest woman is Kishimoto
OL,15,FFuyo, a 114-year-old from Kyoto City
OL,16,Fand the oldest man is Kato Hikaru, a
OL,17,F112-year-old from Kumamoto.
OL,23,APub: 15-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
