OL,3,AMore than 100,000 people in Japan are
OL,4,Anow aged 100 or older
OL,5,
OL,6,FHealth Minister Kenichiro Ueno said he
OL,7,Fwas "delighted that so many people are
OL,8,Fliving long, healthy and active lives",
OL,9,Fciting progress in medicine and
OL,10,Ftechnology.
OL,12,FBut Kenichiri also warned of the
OL,13,Fchallenge the country faces in
OL,14,Fmaintaining a sustainable social
OL,15,Fsecurity system.
